---
description: Next.js web app conventions — routing, i18n, components.
globs:
  - web/**
---

Next.js 16 App Router. RSC by default; `"use client"` only when needed (state, effects, browser APIs). Tailwind v4. Biome: tabs, double quotes. Path alias `@/*` → `web/`.

Hard rules:

- Pass the route `locale` to every fetch of a per-language document (`$locale` in GROQ), and `{ locale, siteLocale }` to anything that builds hrefs.
- Select per-language documents in GROQ with `language == $locale`; only the global `siteLanguageSettings` is fetched by `_id`. This is the design on `variant/document-level`, not the "no locale in GROQ" anti-pattern from `main`.
- Fields are plain values in the route's language — render them directly. `web/sanity/utils/sanityLocalizedText.ts` is only used by `resolveLinkLabel` for link titles that arrive as arrays.
- Content blocks are **modules** (see `.cursor/rules/modules.mdc`). No ad-hoc `<section>` in route files.
- Types for Sanity data are generated: wrap full queries in `defineQuery`, run `pnpm generate`, use the names in `web/sanity/types.ts`. No `as` on fetched data.
- Don't set `data-sanity` in module components — `ModulesRenderer` wraps every module with its field-level path, and Visual Editing depends on rendering modules through it.
- Never read locale from `useRouter()`, `usePathname()`, `window.location`, or cookies inside a module — breaks SSR + Presentation iframes.
- No hardcoded locale codes outside `web/src/i18n/`.

URL/locale helpers live in `web/src/i18n/` (`paths.ts`, `siteLocalePathUtils.ts`, `site-locales.ts`, `proxyLocaleFetch.ts`). Use them; do not concatenate locale prefixes by hand.

After web changes:

```
pnpm typecheck
pnpm format
```

NEVER edit:

- `web/.next/`
- Any `*.gen.*` files
- Imports from `studio/...` (use `packages/*` for shared code).
